# NOTE: this file is normally auto-generated — do not hand-maintain it.
#
# feedmill-backend writes /etc/feedmill/io.conf itself (see
# generateIoConf()/syncIoConf() in src/ethercat.ts) from the configured
# Omron rack and every signal currently mapped to an equipment port —
# never edit it by hand, it'll just get overwritten.
#
# CONFIRMED on a real NX-ECC203: the coupler + every NX module racked
# behind it is ONE EtherCAT slave (position 0) — there's no separate bus
# position per card, and a digital card's points all share ONE PDO entry
# (its point count in bits), addressed as a bit within it, not one entry
# each. That's why every "slave" line below is the same coupler, and every
# digital "channel" line carries an explicit bit number as its own field
# (the daemon doesn't compute it from the point number). Nothing here is
# a hand-maintained table: wire a card up, assign its slot in the HMI,
# click Read Rack.
#
# What follows is a worked example of the format the generator produces —
# the two digital lines are REAL values confirmed from `ethercat pdos -p 0`
# against an NX-ECC203 + one NX-OD5256 (16 DO) + one NX-ID5442 (16 DI).
# The AI/AO/SCALE lines are still unverified placeholders (see io_daemon.c's
# header) — analog/scale channels get one whole PDO entry PER channel
# (point field in the signal id selects which), not a shared bit-packed
# word like digital.
cycle_us 4000
state_path /run/feedmill/io-state.json
command_path /run/feedmill/io-command.txt
slave 0 0x00000083 0x00000000
channel O:01.00 0 DO 0x7002 0x01 0
channel O:01.01 0 DO 0x7002 0x01 1
channel I:02.00 0 DI 0x6022 0x01 0
channel I:02.01 0 DI 0x6022 0x01 1 count
channel AI:03.00 0 AI 0x6010 0x01 0
channel AO:03.00 0 AO 0x7010 0x01 0
channel SC:mixer-scale 0 SCALE 0x6020 0x01 0
